// Per-job-type equipment kits — the app's memory of what an electrical job
// actually needs. Injected server-side into the characterization agent as a
// DATA block, so the product list it returns contains the boring parts too:
// glands, end sleeves, labels, fire-stop, warning tape, the second trip.
//
// Kept on the server, not in the browser bundle: ~12KB per family is cheap as
// one prompt block and expensive as a download every user pays for.
//
// Sourced from field practice per family and hardened by an adversarial
// "what did the quote forget" review pass. Stav has the engineering signature.
//
// Job types in the app map onto these families via KIT_FOR_JOB_TYPE.

